From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Keep only the compute arena in a
 compute unit's lease

A compute unit keeps a lease on the VM of the last command that retired
on it until another VM's compute command retires on the same unit. The
lease held the whole VmState, and with it the VM's resource cache: its
compute arena and also its render arena, about 0.9 GB with eight
resident units.

Render leases are displaced by any later render, and the desktop
renders, so they end within a minute. Nothing on a desktop issues
compute, so a client that issued a single compute command, such as a
texture upload that Mesa performs with a compute copy, kept its whole
render arena until reboot. Each such client added about 0.9 GB.

The lease now holds the compute arena itself, which owns everything the
unit's last command named: the compute objects, the VM's binding (page
tables and ASID) and its live token. The VM identity needed for the
retarget record is copied into the lease. The VM state, its render
arena and its context mapping are released with the VM's other
references. Compute commands name neither the render arena nor the
context mapping.

The stats file now lists each held lease by VM id (compute with the
arena size), the PB-slot leases and the open VMs.

Assisted-by: LLM
